# Self-Check — 4 Mechanism Compliance

Run this checklist after every structural change to the template.
**If any check fails, fix the violation before closing the task.**

---

## 1. SSOT — Single Source of Truth

- [ ] Is the changed/added content now present in more than one file?
      Fix: keep the fact in one canonical file; replace all other occurrences with links
- [ ] Is every new `docs/` file registered in `docs/SSOT-map.md`?
      Fix: add the row in the same commit as the new file
- [ ] Does any file repeat a paragraph, table, or list from another file verbatim?
      That is always a violation — one of them must become a link

## 2. Hierarchical Context & Routing

- [ ] Does `CLAUDE.md` contain ONLY Claude Code-specific differences?
      It must NOT contain routing tables — those belong in `AGENT.md`
- [ ] Is `AGENT.md` still the single source for routing logic?
      Any routing change goes in `AGENT.md` only; `CLAUDE.md` links to it
- [ ] Are any new rule or context files referenced in `AGENT.md`'s hierarchy table?

## 3. MDC — Frontmatter Compliance

- [ ] Do all `.mdc` files have a `description` field in frontmatter?
- [ ] Does each `.mdc` have either `globs` (domain-specific) or `alwaysApply: true` (global)?
      A file with neither will never auto-attach — it is effectively dead
- [ ] Is new behavior-constraining content in `.cursor/rules/`?
- [ ] Is new domain-knowledge content in `.cursor/context/`?
      These two directories serve different purposes — do not mix them

## 4. Memory Distillation

- [ ] Was `LEARNINGS.md` written to before distilling anything to rules/skills/ADR/docs?
- [ ] Does every new rule or skill trace back to a real observed task problem, not speculation?

---

> All checks pass → close the task.
> Any check fails → fix first, then re-run this checklist from the top.
